  1562	### 15.8 Spec and vectors object assembly [OWNER 2026-10-14, G13]
  1563	
  1564	Each object is one or more parts. A part is the ASCII line `tessera-v1-part <path> <length>` LF, then exactly
  1565	`<length>` bytes (decimal, no leading zeros), then LF. `<path>` is repository-relative UTF-8 without spaces. Parts are
  1566	in bytewise-sorted path order; file bytes verbatim as committed. The spec object holds the frozen
  1567	`docs/V1-PROFILE.md` and `formal/p8/ENCODING-V1.md` (plus the branch-registration supplement under the hybrid). The
  1568	vectors object holds every file under `formal/p8/vectors/` and the non-P8 conformance vectors (RES §L). The vectors
  1569	may embed the spec hash; the spec never embeds the vectors' hash.
  1570	
  1571	**Canonical recipe** [OWNER 2026-10-14, r2-F13]. Supersedes the header and inventory sentences above where they
  1572	differ.
  1573	- **Header grammar.** `tessera-v1-part` SP `<path>` SP `<length>` LF, with fixed single literal spaces. `<path>` is an
  1574	  ASCII repository-relative path matching `[A-Za-z0-9._/-]+`, with no empty, `.` or `..` component, no leading
  1575	  slash, and unique within the object; `<length>` matches `0|[1-9][0-9]*`.
  1576	- **Bytes.** Only tracked regular-file **blob bytes** from a named freeze commit: no newline conversion, no symlink
  1577	  following, no generated caches, no working-tree overlay.
  1578	- **Inventory.** The freeze record publishes the exact sorted path inventory of each object, including the non-P8
  1579	  conformance vector files (RES §L names cases, not paths), with an assembler and an independent byte-agreement
  1580	  check.
  1581	- **A9 is a part (owner choice).** The spec object also carries the governing A9 bytes
  1582	  (`docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md` at its signing commit) as a part, so the object is the complete archival
  1583	  spec; this was chosen over distributing A9 separately with a bound digest.
  1584	- **Hashes live outside.** Actual spec, vectors and catalog hashes are recorded in a separate release/freeze record
  1585	  **outside** the frozen spec parts; recording them inside an included file would be self-reference.
  1586	- The part format is a new packaging choice, not an inherited P8 construction or a proven archival format. Once
  1587	  exact catalog hashes exist, runtime hash checks are unique; runtime never parses these objects as policy.
  1588	  *(Dated correction 2026-10-14: "repository-relative UTF-8 without spaces" admitted LF, CR, tab, absolute and
  1589	  dot paths and duplicates; "every file under formal/p8/vectors/" did not select tracked regular files; "the
  1590	  non-P8 conformance vectors (RES §L)" named cases, not files.)*
