    26	
    27	### F01 — MEDIUM: the empirical conclusions drop the censoring and clock qualifications
    28	
    29	**Locations:** A10 :73–74, :257–271; evidence :95–110 and :149–152.
    30	
    31	The measurements reproduce. The limitations are candidly recorded in the technical body, but the interpretation says A-UTC held and the plain summary says measurements found no six-block failure. Those are stronger statements than this dataset establishes. The dataset rejects arrivals outside ±7200 seconds of header time, and no lower bound on observer clock error is supplied. Taking the earliest observer arrival can select a slow clock. Propagation delay alone makes arrival lag conservative; an unbounded negative clock error does not.
