    33	- Codex MCP server tables are `[mcp_servers.<server-name>]`; `[mcp_server.qhaway]` was ignored. After changing the Tessera config to `[mcp_servers.qhaway]`, `codex mcp list` showed qhaway enabled, and direct initialization exposed `recall` and `remember`. [Task 1]
    34	- `enabled_tools` is optional; when present it is an exact-name allow list. khipumaq advertised `search`, `recall`, and `describe`, while its inherited list named obsolete `search_history` and `open_episode`; setting `enabled_tools = ["search", "recall", "describe"]` exposed all three. [Task 2]
